# Vouched contributors for hyperdxio/hyperdx.
#
# Pull requests from GitHub users who are not in this list are closed
# automatically by .github/workflows/vouch.yml. See CONTRIBUTING.md for how to
# get vouched — it is deliberately easy.
#
# Org members and anyone else with write access are allowed regardless of this
# list. The team is listed anyway so the file reads as a complete roster.
#
# Maintainers manage the list by commenting on any issue or PR:
#   /vouch @user [reason]
#   /denounce @user [reason]
#   /unvouch @user
#
# Syntax (https://github.com/mitchellh/vouch):
#   - One entry per line: a handle without @, sorted alphabetically, lower case.
#     Vouch lower-cases handles when it rewrites the file, and matching is
#     case-insensitive, so seeding lower-case keeps bot edits to one line.
#   - Anything after the handle and a space is free-text detail, not part of
#     the handle. The reason from `/vouch @user reason` is stored there, so a
#     line like `jane wants to fix the timezone bug` is one vouched user.
#   - Denounce with a leading minus: -username [reason]
#   - Optional platform prefix: github:username
#
# Seeded from the hyperdxio org plus every external contributor with two or
# more merged pull requests as of August 2026.
#
# copilot is listed because vouch only auto-exempts logins ending in "[bot]".
# GitHub's Copilot coding agent has the login "Copilot", so without an entry
# its PRs would be closed.
